  "notes": "Compound of {想|そう} (think, imagine) + {起|き} (arise). A formal word primarily used in writing. In everyday speech, {思|おも}い{出|だ}す is far more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {想起|そうき}する — to recall, to recollect (する verb)\n- {想起|そうき}させる — to remind someone of, to evoke\n- {記憶|きおく}の{想起|そうき} — memory recall\n- {想起|そうき}{訓練|くんれん} — recall training\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {思|おも}い{出|だ}す — to remember, to recall (everyday word)\n- {回想|かいそう} — reminiscence, looking back (slightly literary)\n- {追憶|ついおく} — reminiscence, recollection (literary/poetic)\n- {連想|れんそう} — association (thinking of one thing from another)",
